    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65946" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελεδ-αίνω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>care for, be cumbered
			about</i>, c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					1129
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2
			</span></i> (Sigeum, <span class="entity">vi B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				10.52
			</span></i>: c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆμαι κακὴν
				οὐ μελεδαίνει ἐσθλὸς ἀνήρ</span> a well-born man
				<i>does</i> not <i>mind</i> marrying a woman of mean birth,
				<i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				185
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>care for, attend upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τοὺς νοσέοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.115
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ὑστέρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					1.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἄνθρωπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					2.10
				</span></i>
			.</div>
